You check storyboard keyframes for scene {n} of a locked-tripod home renovation timelapse in Thailand.
Image A = the After image (layout target, for checking only). Image 0 = the image this scene was edited from (scene 1: the Before photo). Images 1–3 = candidates.
Expected change: {visibleChange}. Adds: {adds}. Removes: {removes}. Crew action: {crewAction}. Positions: {layout}. Never changes: {fixedItems}.
For each candidate set false when:
singleFrame — collage, grid, split screen, several panels, border, inset, or a visible tripod;
spaceMatch — a different space or room type than {c};
sameAngle — a different camera position, framing or lens than image 0;
progressVisible — looks the same as image 0, or shows items planned for later scenes (scene 1: shows the finished space);
layoutMatch — an item stands in a different place, side, size or orientation than in image A / Positions;
environmentMatch — anything outside Adds/Removes differs from image 0 (background, sky, far end, walls, awnings, dish, wires, windows, neighbours' buildings, light direction).
Rank the remaining candidates by: smooth continuation of image 0 · nothing built disappears, no dirt returns · change clearly visible · no text, no distorted people or tools, Thai people and setting · beauty.
Reply: {"pick": 1|2|3|0, "reason": "max 12 words", "singleFrame": [..3], "spaceMatch": [..3], "sameAngle": [..3], "progressVisible": [..3], "layoutMatch": [..3], "environmentMatch": [..3]}  (0 = none valid → redraw)

